WEBVTT

00:02.024 --> 00:04.109
Previously on lost:

00:06.153 --> 00:09.656
Right now, this is our priority.

00:15.621 --> 00:17.915
How did you come to be
on this island?

00:17.998 --> 00:21.335
The ship slammed into rocks,
ran aground.

00:39.895 --> 00:42.189
Hold on a second, dude.
You want what now?

00:45.567 --> 00:48.320
You wanna make snowballs?
— hold the bamboo tighter.

00:52.157 --> 00:53.533
Hey. — hey.

00:53.617 --> 00:55.869
How's it coming? — it's coming.

00:55.953 --> 00:58.580
Long as nobody sabotages
this one as well.

00:58.664 --> 01:00.791
I got people standing guard 24/7.

01:00.874 --> 01:04.002
Nobody gets near this,
with or without intent to burn.

01:04.086 --> 01:06.672
I was thinking,
the chances of a passing ship

01:06.755 --> 01:09.091
spotting this raft out there
is pretty slim.

01:09.174 --> 01:11.593
We could use something
to send a distress call

01:11.677 --> 01:14.221
to any ship that might be close.
Like an sos.

01:14.304 --> 01:17.933
I'll ask Sayid, but even if he could
make something like that,

01:18.016 --> 01:20.310
he's not gonna have anything
to power it with.

01:20.394 --> 01:23.272
Didn't Sayid say that crazy
French chick had batteries?

01:25.607 --> 01:28.402
Absolutely not.
— I'm not asking you to go.

01:28.485 --> 01:29.987
I'll do it. — no, you won't.

01:30.070 --> 01:32.197
We're trying...
— do you think she would

01:32.281 --> 01:34.491
give up something she needs
to a stranger?

01:34.574 --> 01:38.161
All I'm asking is for you
to tell me how to find her. That's it.

01:38.245 --> 01:40.622
I was brought unconscious to her camp.

01:40.706 --> 01:43.625
I was disoriented.
I don't know how to find her.

01:43.709 --> 01:45.711
Don't know, dude?
Or don't want to?

01:46.712 --> 01:49.464
Sayid, look. You've got
her maps and her papers.

01:49.548 --> 01:51.967
You thought they were
pointing to something.

01:52.050 --> 01:54.594
I was wrong.
— maybe they're pointing to her.

01:54.678 --> 01:56.722
I don't know what these papers mean!

01:56.805 --> 01:59.474
They could be the ravings
of her disturbed mind.

01:59.558 --> 02:01.852
Song lyrics, mixed with equations!

02:07.065 --> 02:08.942
Ifthis map is pointing to her,

02:09.026 --> 02:11.987
then you should know
she resides here in this area.

02:12.070 --> 02:15.324
She gave it a name.
Territoire foncé.

02:15.407 --> 02:16.742
Shannon translated it.

02:16.825 --> 02:21.621
It means "dark territory." That sound
like a place you'd like to visit?

02:21.705 --> 02:24.833
So you won't help?
— I didn't say that.

02:24.916 --> 02:28.879
I'll build the distress beacon.
I suggest you find another power source.

02:28.962 --> 02:32.632
Something in the cockpit.
— we're not going to the cockpit.

02:37.429 --> 02:39.431
Swing your partner, dosey do

02:39.514 --> 02:42.267
step high!
— Hugo, what are you doing in there?

02:42.351 --> 02:45.979
When you out the...
— I'm just checking something out.

02:46.063 --> 02:49.524
I hope you're not watching those
g—string mujeres again.

02:49.608 --> 02:51.234
Look, ma, we talked about this.

02:51.318 --> 02:54.571
If you want me living here,
you gotta respect my privacy.

02:55.280 --> 02:56.740
And no, I'm not.

02:59.117 --> 03:02.662
Look at you.
It's Saturday night.

03:02.746 --> 03:06.708
A grown—up man
sitting at home watching TV.

03:06.792 --> 03:10.128
You should go out.
Try to find yourself a nice woman.

03:10.212 --> 03:11.546
I'll get right on that.

03:11.630 --> 03:14.424
Try eating better.
You're gaining weight again.

03:14.508 --> 03:17.219
With the mega number 42.

03:20.263 --> 03:23.767
And that makes tonight's
mega lotto jackpot drawing

03:23.850 --> 03:29.106
four, eight, 15, 16 and 23,

03:29.189 --> 03:31.358
with the mega number 42.

03:31.441 --> 03:34.152
Whoever has those numbers has won

03:34.236 --> 03:37.030
or will share
in a near record jackpot.

03:37.114 --> 03:41.326
That's right, Mary Jo, because this
is the sixteenth week without a winner.

04:17.028 --> 04:18.572
You awake?

04:18.655 --> 04:20.949
I was just wondering that myself.

04:23.660 --> 04:25.704
That French lady wrote this stuff?

04:26.371 --> 04:29.082
It's the middle of the night.
What do you want?

04:29.166 --> 04:32.127
Nothing. Couldn't sleep.

04:32.210 --> 04:34.963
And I got curious.

04:35.046 --> 04:36.756
You and Shannon,

04:36.840 --> 04:39.968
you guys have been trying
to figure out some of this stuff,

04:40.051 --> 04:43.013
and I was wondering what...

04:43.096 --> 04:46.516
You guys figured out
about this stuff?

04:47.809 --> 04:50.270
What stuff? — I don't know.

04:50.353 --> 04:53.356
Well, take these numbers
she wrote down a bunch of times.

04:55.442 --> 04:56.860
Got any idea what it means?

04:59.779 --> 05:02.991
I thought at one time they might be
coordinates of some kind.

05:03.074 --> 05:05.160
Coordinates, yeah.

05:06.578 --> 05:09.789
But when you first found her,
the French chick,

05:09.873 --> 05:12.792
you said you saw a wire
or something on the beach.

05:12.876 --> 05:14.836
You followed it,
and it led you to her.

05:14.920 --> 05:18.131
No. It led me into a trap she set.

05:18.215 --> 05:20.217
But her place is probably close, right?

05:21.843 --> 05:25.096
Why are you interested in Rousseau?
— I'm not.

05:25.180 --> 05:27.516
Just making conversation, dude.

05:27.599 --> 05:29.768
Sorry if it's a bad time.

05:31.102 --> 05:32.437
Good night.

05:44.115 --> 05:45.200
Yeah, you.

05:45.283 --> 05:48.286
How did you come up
with the winning numbers?

05:49.913 --> 05:53.416
They just sorta came to me.

05:53.500 --> 05:57.546
Why don't you introduce your family?
— oh, yeah, okay.

05:57.629 --> 06:01.424
This bashful beauty is my mom, Carmen.
Come here, ma.

06:02.092 --> 06:05.428
And this is my brother, Diego,
and his wife, Lisa.

06:05.512 --> 06:07.597
We're rich! — nice, dude.

06:07.681 --> 06:09.766
Ignore him. He's an idiot. And...

06:10.892 --> 06:14.104
You gotta meet this guy.
This is the greatest guy I know.

06:14.187 --> 06:18.900
My grandpa, tito.
He's worked three jobs for...

06:18.984 --> 06:21.236
How long's it been, abuelito?
— 52 years.

06:21.319 --> 06:22.571
Fifty—two years!

06:22.654 --> 06:26.157
He's 70 years old, and the closest thing
that he's had to a vacation

06:26.241 --> 06:29.244
is when they put a pacemaker
in him four years ago.

06:29.327 --> 06:33.707
The first thing I'll do with the money
is to give him the rest he's earned.

06:33.790 --> 06:35.625
That's what it's all about for me,

06:35.709 --> 06:39.504
to be able to do things
for the people I care about.

06:39.588 --> 06:42.549
'Cause I really put my family
through a lot recently,

06:42.632 --> 06:45.719
and, well, this way
I can make it up to them.

06:45.802 --> 06:50.432
You know, maybe even
buy my mom a new house.

06:50.515 --> 06:53.768
And maybe after my grandpa
comes back from his cruise,

06:53.852 --> 06:58.523
we can get to do some of the things
that we always wanted to do.

07:01.318 --> 07:02.819
Grandpa?

07:08.450 --> 07:10.118
Hey. — I'm not doing anything.

07:10.201 --> 07:11.620
What?

07:13.204 --> 07:15.123
What?
— just saying good morning.

07:16.082 --> 07:17.709
Oh. Right.

07:17.792 --> 07:18.918
Morning.

07:19.878 --> 07:21.796
Sorry. — you going somewhere?

07:21.880 --> 07:23.173
Me? No.

07:25.467 --> 07:27.385
Well, yeah...

07:28.803 --> 07:30.722
Just thought I might take a walk.

07:31.723 --> 07:34.809
Maybe scope out some new fishing area.

07:34.893 --> 07:36.519
I'll come with. — that's okay.

07:36.603 --> 07:38.313
I could use a bit of the wide open.

07:38.396 --> 07:41.733
Dude, I could really use
some alone time right now.

07:42.817 --> 07:43.943
Sure.

07:53.411 --> 07:56.039
I'm a big guy.
I get dehydrated easy.

07:59.709 --> 08:00.794
Yeah, okay.

08:08.635 --> 08:12.180
Claire, you got a second?

08:12.931 --> 08:14.974
Sure.
— I was wondering if you're free

08:15.058 --> 08:16.810
to help me with a little project.

08:18.603 --> 08:22.023
I'm building something and I could
use an extra pair of hands.

08:22.107 --> 08:25.276
I'm nine months pregnant.
I can barely waddle to the beach.

08:25.360 --> 08:26.611
Could you hold a saw?

08:29.906 --> 08:32.325
Yeah.
— can you move your hand back and forth?

08:34.452 --> 08:36.538
Possibly. — you're perfect.

08:37.288 --> 08:38.498
Come on.

08:41.084 --> 08:42.460
Okay.

08:48.133 --> 08:51.511
So, what exactly are we building?

08:54.639 --> 08:55.724
Where is it?

08:58.768 --> 09:01.771
Where's what?
— the map. It won't help you find her.

09:01.855 --> 09:03.565
I don't have it. — what's worse

09:03.648 --> 09:06.568
is you won't do your own dirty work.
You get Hurley to do it.

09:06.651 --> 09:08.570
Wait a minute. Hurley?

09:08.653 --> 09:11.573
He was in my tent last night.
Quizzing me about Rousseau.

09:11.656 --> 09:14.743
About numbers she wrote,
how I came to find her.

09:17.912 --> 09:20.206
You don't know anything
about this, do you?

09:22.000 --> 09:24.502
Charlie, have you seen Hurley?

09:25.462 --> 09:28.173
Couple of hours ago.
He was setting out for a walk.

09:28.256 --> 09:29.924
Acting like a loon, I might add.

09:31.676 --> 09:33.595
My god. He's going after her.

09:34.929 --> 09:39.142
When are you gonna be back?
— If we catch him, before nightfall.

09:39.225 --> 09:40.518
Why?

09:41.019 --> 09:42.353
Are you worried about me?

09:43.897 --> 09:44.981
So what if I am?

09:47.692 --> 09:49.277
Sayid!

09:49.360 --> 09:50.612
You ready?

09:56.326 --> 09:58.411
I'll be fine.

10:18.264 --> 10:20.308
Hugo, turn that noise down.

10:20.391 --> 10:22.685
Oh, sorry.

10:25.688 --> 10:28.817
Where are you taking me?
You know I don't like surprises.

10:28.900 --> 10:30.985
You're gonna like this one, ma.

10:31.069 --> 10:33.738
I mean, after everything
you've been through...

10:33.822 --> 10:35.281
Like grandpa...

10:38.910 --> 10:42.747
Then at the funeral, father aguilar
getting struck by lightning.

10:43.915 --> 10:45.542
Man, that was a freak storm.

10:46.209 --> 10:47.961
And Diego moving back home

10:48.044 --> 10:52.674
after Lisa left him for that waitress.
— don't mention that whore.

10:52.757 --> 10:55.593
I'm just saying, you deserve
something good to happen.

11:00.807 --> 11:03.101
You know,

11:03.184 --> 11:05.603
ever since I won the lottery,
it's like...

11:07.146 --> 11:09.691
We've had nothing but bad luck.

11:10.608 --> 11:12.443
Like, I don't know,

11:12.527 --> 11:14.320
the money's cursed or something.

11:15.613 --> 11:18.366
That's blasphemy.
You know we are catholic.

11:18.449 --> 11:21.995
We don't believe in curses.
— ma, I'm just talking.

11:24.455 --> 11:27.000
Okay, we're almost there.
Here, put this on.

11:43.057 --> 11:46.060
Why do I have to wear this?
— give me your hand. Careful.

11:46.144 --> 11:47.937
You be careful. — stepping down.

11:48.021 --> 11:49.981
I can't see anything.

11:51.316 --> 11:54.527
Okay, now,
take off your blindfold,

11:54.611 --> 11:57.655
and get a look at
your new dream house.

11:57.739 --> 11:59.532
My ankle.

11:59.991 --> 12:02.160
I said take off your blindfold.

12:02.243 --> 12:04.704
Why did you make me
put that thing on?

12:08.291 --> 12:09.834
Do I smell smoke?

12:11.252 --> 12:12.921
Crap!

12:13.004 --> 12:14.464
Hang on. I gotta call 911.

12:14.547 --> 12:17.008
You tell them I broke my ankle.

12:26.267 --> 12:28.478
Drop the phone.
Move away from the vehicle.

12:28.561 --> 12:30.605
It's the house. — do it! Now!

12:30.688 --> 12:32.065
Turn around.

12:36.194 --> 12:38.154
No such thing as curses, ma?

12:39.155 --> 12:41.032
You have the right to remain silent.

12:41.115 --> 12:44.452
Anything you say can and will
be used against you.

13:01.928 --> 13:03.721
French chick!

13:12.063 --> 13:13.773
I would think you'd be happy.

13:13.856 --> 13:15.483
Every one of your stocks is up.

13:15.566 --> 13:18.486
Your interests in orange futures
skyrocketed

13:18.569 --> 13:20.989
after those tropical storms hit Florida.

13:21.072 --> 13:24.492
And you are now
the majority shareholder

13:24.575 --> 13:28.079
for a box company in tustin.

13:28.162 --> 13:30.748
A box company?
— they make boxes.

13:30.832 --> 13:33.918
Lucrative business.
Everybody needs boxes.

13:34.002 --> 13:37.338
Which reminds me,
your sneaker factory in Canada...

13:37.422 --> 13:40.842
I own a sneaker factory in Canada?
— well, not anymore.

13:40.925 --> 13:45.430
It was destroyed in a fire last month.
— of course it was.

13:45.513 --> 13:48.891
You might have read about it.
Eight—something people died.

13:48.975 --> 13:51.519
But the good news is,
we over—insured it.

13:51.602 --> 13:53.479
It's gonna yield you a windfall.

13:53.563 --> 13:57.233
And when we add in the generous
settlement from the LAPD

13:57.316 --> 14:00.695
for your false arrest,
you've almost doubled your net worth

14:00.778 --> 14:01.904
in a few short months.

14:01.988 --> 14:05.575
I still can't imagine how the police
mistook you for a drug dealer.

14:08.202 --> 14:10.913
You are not the first
lottery winner to believe

14:10.997 --> 14:14.167
the money's brought nothing but trouble.
It's in your head.

14:14.250 --> 14:16.753
You don't believe in jinxes?
You know, curses?

14:16.836 --> 14:19.005
I'm an accountant.
I believe in numbers.

14:19.088 --> 14:21.549
Where'd you get 'em, anyway?
— what?

14:21.632 --> 14:24.385
The numbers. What did you use?
Somebody's birthday?

14:24.469 --> 14:28.473
Phone number?
— It's nothing. It's just something...

14:31.726 --> 14:33.019
What?

14:37.315 --> 14:39.609
It's not the money,
it's the numbers.

14:39.692 --> 14:40.985
The numbers are cursed.

14:42.278 --> 14:44.405
Don't look at me like that.
I'm not crazy.

14:44.489 --> 14:46.824
This is really...
— listen to yourself.

14:46.991 --> 14:50.703
"The numbers are cursed."
You know there is no such thing as...

15:05.009 --> 15:06.844
You wanna hit that a little harder?

15:08.471 --> 15:12.266
I'm sorry. Is my building a raft
to get us rescued bothering you?

15:12.350 --> 15:15.269
At the moment, yeah.
— why aren't you helping?

15:15.353 --> 15:17.438
I am helping, short—round.

15:17.522 --> 15:19.190
Keeping watch for arsonists.

15:19.982 --> 15:21.984
Walt's got a point.

15:22.068 --> 15:25.530
You could pitch in,
as you've already bought your ticket.

15:30.243 --> 15:33.538
Did you tie this like I told you?
If you'd tied it like I told you,

15:33.621 --> 15:35.790
the thing would still be together.

15:35.873 --> 15:39.544
What's the matter with you?
What is your problem?

15:42.880 --> 15:45.049
He's never going
to speak to me again.

15:46.801 --> 15:47.969
He just needs time.

15:50.138 --> 15:52.974
I humiliated him.

15:59.147 --> 16:02.567
When the raft sails,

16:02.650 --> 16:05.236
do you think he's going
to leave with them?

16:07.238 --> 16:08.739
I don't know.

16:49.280 --> 16:50.656
Don't move!

16:51.866 --> 16:54.368
Hey, what are you guys...?
— do not move.

16:54.452 --> 16:56.329
You're on a pressure trigger.

16:56.412 --> 16:59.540
If you take your weight off it,
it will release that.

17:04.295 --> 17:05.546
Oh, man.

17:07.632 --> 17:10.301
We need to replace
his weight on the trigger.

17:10.384 --> 17:13.179
How we gonna do that?
— don't move.

17:13.262 --> 17:15.223
Hey, everybody just calm down.

17:15.306 --> 17:17.683
Can I drop the wire?
— maybe I'll find a rock.

17:17.767 --> 17:19.602
I'm dropping the wire. — no!

17:23.856 --> 17:25.608
I can make it. — don't move.

17:25.691 --> 17:27.693
I can get out of the way.
I'm spry.

17:27.777 --> 17:29.654
Stay put. — no, wait!

17:30.071 --> 17:31.197
Don't even...

17:37.119 --> 17:39.747
Hurley, what the bloody hell's
wrong with you?

17:39.830 --> 17:41.958
Nothing.

17:44.377 --> 17:45.878
What are you doing out here?

17:46.587 --> 17:47.964
I came to get a battery.

17:49.048 --> 17:51.842
Seriously, what's going on?

17:54.136 --> 17:55.596
You guys coming?

18:00.017 --> 18:02.937
You all want to go? Fine.

18:03.521 --> 18:06.190
But perhaps I should take the lead.

18:06.274 --> 18:08.359
Excellent notion.

18:14.365 --> 18:16.742
Lenny. His name is Lenny.

18:16.826 --> 18:19.704
Or Leonard.
— but you don't know his last name.

18:19.787 --> 18:22.415
Look, I just need to talk to him
for five minutes.

18:22.498 --> 18:24.500
If you can't tell me
the person's name,

18:24.583 --> 18:27.670
I can't look it up.
— how many leonards are here?

18:27.753 --> 18:29.630
Can't you just type in "Leonard"?

18:29.714 --> 18:32.591
The guy's been here forever.
He knows me.

18:32.675 --> 18:35.303
Our records are private,
and any visitors...

18:35.386 --> 18:37.888
Dude, do not do that right now!

18:37.972 --> 18:41.183
Leave the bulb for another time, man.

18:46.731 --> 18:48.149
Five minutes.

18:48.232 --> 18:50.943
All I need is five minutes.

18:52.903 --> 18:55.656
Oh, hey, doc.
— It's good to see you!

18:55.740 --> 18:57.283
What are you doing back here?

19:01.996 --> 19:05.207
I don't remember you and Leonard
being that close, Hugo.

19:06.083 --> 19:08.336
Yeah. Well, we hung.

19:09.086 --> 19:11.339
I'll leave you gentlemen to it.

19:11.422 --> 19:13.466
Good luck, Hugo.

19:19.847 --> 19:21.307
Hey, Lenny.

19:22.308 --> 19:23.768
Remember me?

19:26.270 --> 19:27.813
Hugo.

19:29.690 --> 19:31.192
Hurley.

19:33.444 --> 19:35.488
Well, I was...

19:35.571 --> 19:38.699
Just, you know,
in the neighborhood and...

19:44.121 --> 19:48.000
Look, Lenny, I gotta know,
what do the numbers mean?

19:48.084 --> 19:51.212
4—8—1516—23—42.

19:58.135 --> 20:00.471
Come on, Lenny,
give me something.

20:00.554 --> 20:03.307
Anything.
Where'd you get the numbers?

20:05.935 --> 20:08.562
Is that why you're here?

20:08.646 --> 20:10.231
It's 'cause of the numbers?

20:10.314 --> 20:12.191
Did they do something to you?

20:12.983 --> 20:15.528
'Cause I think
they did something to me.

20:16.487 --> 20:19.490
I think they turned me into a jinx.

20:20.616 --> 20:22.868
Bad news to everyone around me.

20:22.952 --> 20:25.246
And when I tell people
I think I'm the cause,

20:26.831 --> 20:29.417
they look at me like I'm nuts.

20:29.500 --> 20:32.253
They don't believe me.
But, I know.

20:32.336 --> 20:35.047
Ever since I won the lottery
with those numbers...

20:40.928 --> 20:44.557
You used those numbers
to play the lottery?

20:49.228 --> 20:51.647
Yeah.
— you shouldn't have done that.

20:52.982 --> 20:55.609
You've opened the box. — I what?

20:55.693 --> 20:57.736
- — You shouldn't have used those!
- Why?

20:57.820 --> 21:00.739
It doesn't stop!
You gotta get away from those numbers.

21:00.823 --> 21:03.617
You gotta get far away.
— all right. Slow down.

21:03.701 --> 21:05.119
Don't you understand?

21:05.202 --> 21:07.621
You gotta get away from them
or it won't stop.

21:07.705 --> 21:09.707
Calm down.
— wait. I need answers.

21:09.790 --> 21:11.542
Step away. — the numbers!

21:11.625 --> 21:14.211
Where'd you get 'em?
— Sam toomey. He heard them.

21:14.295 --> 21:16.255
He heard them in kalgoorlie.

21:16.338 --> 21:18.549
What's kalgoorlie?
— It's a town.

21:18.632 --> 21:22.303
A town where? — in Australia.

21:22.386 --> 21:24.221
Oh, god.

21:26.807 --> 21:28.434
It stops here.

21:28.517 --> 21:30.436
It goes into the ground.

21:32.396 --> 21:34.148
This poses somewhat of a problem.

21:34.231 --> 21:37.526
Guys, you should come see this.

21:57.463 --> 22:01.467
You never mentioned a bridge.
— I never saw this before.

22:02.259 --> 22:06.055
No way she could have built this.
— no, but her team could have.

22:06.138 --> 22:07.932
Or Ethan's team.

22:10.518 --> 22:13.521
What are you doing?
— relax, I'm just gonna check it out.

22:13.604 --> 22:15.689
You guys stay here.
— get back here!

22:15.773 --> 22:17.983
Dudes, chill.

23:01.527 --> 23:02.611
If he can do it...

23:44.361 --> 23:45.529
Dude, you okay?

23:47.990 --> 23:49.992
I'm okay.

23:50.993 --> 23:52.369
You two stay right there.

23:52.453 --> 23:55.039
We'll find a way around,
and we'll meet you there.

23:55.122 --> 23:57.333
Screw that! You guys stay!

23:57.416 --> 23:59.043
There's a path right here.

23:59.126 --> 24:02.171
Will you shut up and listen to Jack.
He said stay put.

24:02.254 --> 24:04.423
You're acting like a bloody lunatic.

24:19.480 --> 24:22.775
If this weren't the middle of nowhere,
I'd say you were lost.

24:22.858 --> 24:26.236
Hi. Is this Sam toomey's house?
— It is. I'm his wife.

24:26.320 --> 24:28.072
Well, is he around?

24:28.155 --> 24:30.824
'Cause I'd kinda like to talk to him.

24:30.908 --> 24:32.660
I'd like that too,

24:32.743 --> 24:35.454
but Sam's been dead for four years.

24:38.082 --> 24:41.669
Your husband worked
with a guy I know, Leonard Simms.

24:41.752 --> 24:45.172
That's right.
They served together in the us. Navy.

24:45.255 --> 24:46.965
How is Leonard?

24:47.049 --> 24:48.759
Still in the service?

24:49.385 --> 24:53.347
He's... retired.

24:55.099 --> 24:58.852
Anyway, he told me about Sam...

24:58.936 --> 25:00.396
Hearing something.

25:03.399 --> 25:05.859
You're talking about the numbers.
— yes.

25:05.943 --> 25:07.820
The numbers. Exactly.

25:07.903 --> 25:10.280
Do you know anything about them?

25:11.699 --> 25:15.285
Sam and Leonard were stationed
at a listening post

25:15.369 --> 25:18.872
monitoring long—wave transmissions
out of the pacific.

25:18.956 --> 25:21.417
Boring job. Sam hated it.

25:22.292 --> 25:25.462
Nothing to do but listen to static,
night after night.

25:25.546 --> 25:30.300
Until one night,
about 16 years ago,

25:30.384 --> 25:32.177
there's something in the static.

25:33.053 --> 25:34.680
A voice comes through,

25:34.763 --> 25:38.225
a voice repeating those numbers

25:38.308 --> 25:39.768
over and over again.

25:43.647 --> 25:47.526
Couple of days later,
we're at the fair in kalgoorlie,

25:47.609 --> 25:51.613
and some Wally there's got this jar,
must have been big as a pony.

25:51.697 --> 25:55.576
It's filled to the rim with beans.
Fella's offering 50 grand to anyone

25:55.659 --> 25:59.955
able to guess how many beans
were in thatjar within ten.

26:00.873 --> 26:03.083
Sam used the numbers. — yep.

26:03.167 --> 26:06.545
The answer was exact to the bean.

26:07.337 --> 26:10.841
Man had been running
the same scam for 40 years,

26:10.924 --> 26:13.093
nobody had ever come close.

26:14.219 --> 26:16.096
So we won the money.

26:16.180 --> 26:20.934
On the way home, a pickup truck
blows a tire on the highway,

26:21.018 --> 26:22.853
hits us head—on.

26:23.771 --> 26:26.106
Lost my leg that night.

26:28.025 --> 26:30.819
What about Sam?
— barely a scratch.

26:31.445 --> 26:34.782
Most people would consider
themselves lucky,

26:34.865 --> 26:36.909
but not him.

26:37.993 --> 26:40.162
He was never the same after that.

26:41.163 --> 26:43.540
He started keeping a record.

26:45.083 --> 26:48.796
Anything terrible that happened
to anyone around us,

26:48.879 --> 26:51.965
he believed it was all
because he used those numbers.

26:52.049 --> 26:55.928
He moved us out here in the middle
of nowhere, hoping it would stop.

26:56.011 --> 26:57.054
Did it?

26:58.722 --> 27:00.641
Did he ever find a way
to make it stop?

27:02.142 --> 27:03.310
Yep.

27:05.479 --> 27:08.232
He put a shotgun in his mouth
and pulled the trigger.

27:11.318 --> 27:14.196
What is it you're looking for,
Mr. Reyes?

27:19.910 --> 27:21.411
I used them.

27:23.080 --> 27:24.790
The numbers.

27:25.457 --> 27:27.417
To win the lottery.

27:30.087 --> 27:33.841
And now I think
I'm under the same curse.

27:33.924 --> 27:37.344
Curse? There's no curse.

27:37.427 --> 27:40.138
You just told me...
— you think I'd still have my leg

27:40.222 --> 27:42.891
if Sam hadn't have picked
the right number of beans?

27:42.975 --> 27:44.643
Floods wouldn't have happened?

27:44.726 --> 27:47.729
Homes wouldn't have burned?
People wouldn't have died?

27:50.941 --> 27:53.068
Well... yeah.

27:53.777 --> 27:57.489
You make your own luck, Mr. Reyes.

27:57.573 --> 28:00.868
Don't blame it on the damn numbers.

28:00.951 --> 28:05.163
You're looking for an excuse
that doesn't exist.

28:09.042 --> 28:11.253
It's a trap, right?

28:11.336 --> 28:13.922
For catching animals?

28:14.715 --> 28:16.091
Pass me that cup, please.

28:19.344 --> 28:21.847
What's this gunk? — glue.

28:22.389 --> 28:24.558
Where'd you find glue?

28:24.641 --> 28:28.103
I made it out of
rendered animal fat.

28:28.812 --> 28:30.522
You made glue?

28:34.610 --> 28:39.448
You should have one of those shows
where you fix up houses for people.

28:47.664 --> 28:50.500
Thanks for this.

28:50.584 --> 28:52.878
Giving me something to do.

28:55.339 --> 28:59.676
I'm tired of trying to remember
what happened to me out there.

29:01.803 --> 29:03.180
How's that coming...

29:05.766 --> 29:07.351
Your memory?

29:07.434 --> 29:09.978
Bits and pieces. Here and there.

29:10.938 --> 29:13.398
Nothing that makes any real sense.

29:14.900 --> 29:16.652
Well, maybe I can help.

29:18.362 --> 29:22.491
I'm good at putting
bits and pieces together.

29:45.681 --> 29:47.140
What?

29:47.224 --> 29:49.434
This is familiar. This area.

29:50.769 --> 29:52.312
We're close.

29:53.438 --> 29:55.065
How do you know?

29:55.732 --> 29:57.693
I thought she lived underground.

30:03.198 --> 30:04.866
What the hell was that?

30:17.587 --> 30:19.506
Hell of a security system.

30:19.589 --> 30:22.509
Somebody trips a wire,
and the whole place blows up.

30:22.592 --> 30:25.095
There's nothing here.
— the batteries?

30:25.178 --> 30:27.097
Nothing.

30:28.724 --> 30:29.808
I don't get it.

30:33.562 --> 30:34.938
She knew.

30:35.897 --> 30:38.900
She knew that one day
I'd come back and bring others.

30:39.609 --> 30:41.987
So she abandoned this place,

30:42.070 --> 30:44.906
booby—trapped it and moved on.

30:46.241 --> 30:48.577
Moved on where?

30:48.660 --> 30:50.912
Jack! Sayid!

30:52.497 --> 30:54.041
Do we know where we're going?

30:54.124 --> 30:56.376
The blast sounded like
it came from this way.

30:56.460 --> 30:58.837
I think. — you don't know.

30:58.920 --> 31:01.006
Dude, what do you want from me?

31:01.089 --> 31:04.551
What do I want? To know what
we're doing in the middle of nowhere.

31:04.634 --> 31:07.220
And don't tell me
it's because of some batteries.

31:07.304 --> 31:09.473
One minute you're
"good—time Hurley."

31:09.556 --> 31:11.224
The next you're colonel Kurtz.

31:11.308 --> 31:14.019
It just doesn't make any sense.
It's not you.

31:14.102 --> 31:15.479
You don't know me.

31:15.562 --> 31:18.565
All this time, you've told me
nothing about yourself.

31:18.648 --> 31:21.568
We all got personal stuff.
— don't change the subject.

31:21.651 --> 31:23.111
We're lost out here.

31:23.195 --> 31:25.238
Jack and Sayid could be hurt,

31:25.322 --> 31:28.158
all because you're acting
like some bloody nutter.

31:30.160 --> 31:32.496
I am not crazy!

31:34.748 --> 31:38.960
I've got my reasons for every...
— I think I have a right to know.

31:42.130 --> 31:43.590
Okay.

31:43.673 --> 31:46.134
All right, you wanna know?
— yeah.

31:48.011 --> 31:50.347
About a year ago...

31:55.018 --> 31:56.978
Is someone shooting at us?

32:20.877 --> 32:23.380
You must be the French chick.
— who are you?

32:23.505 --> 32:24.840
Hurley.

32:29.344 --> 32:32.389
Sayid, that guy you tortured...

32:33.890 --> 32:35.392
You were on the plane.

32:36.351 --> 32:39.896
Look, I came here to find... easy.

32:43.066 --> 32:45.026
I'm just getting your notes.

32:52.576 --> 32:56.163
Please, tell me why you wrote this.

32:56.246 --> 32:58.415
What do these numbers mean?
Please.

33:01.168 --> 33:02.586
I don't know.

33:04.129 --> 33:05.130
What?

33:08.758 --> 33:10.260
You don't know?

33:11.136 --> 33:14.431
Okay, that thing in the woods...

33:16.725 --> 33:18.560
Maybe it's a monster,

33:18.643 --> 33:22.522
maybe it's a pissed—off giraffe.

33:22.606 --> 33:24.858
I don't know.

33:24.941 --> 33:29.196
The fact that no one
is even looking for us,

33:29.279 --> 33:31.781
yeah, that's weird.

33:31.865 --> 33:33.825
But I just go along with it.

33:33.909 --> 33:35.869
'Cause I'm along for the ride.

33:35.952 --> 33:39.372
Good old fun—time Hurley!

33:39.456 --> 33:41.875
Well, guess what?

33:41.958 --> 33:45.921
Now I want some freaking answers!

34:00.769 --> 34:04.648
Our ship picked up a transmission,

34:04.731 --> 34:07.067
a voice, repeating those numbers.

34:07.984 --> 34:10.195
We changed course to investigate.

34:10.820 --> 34:13.740
After we shipwrecked,

34:13.823 --> 34:16.910
my team continued to search
for the transmission source.

34:17.786 --> 34:20.330
It was weeks before
we found the radio tower.

34:20.413 --> 34:22.415
There's a radio tower on this island?

34:22.499 --> 34:25.752
Yes, up by the black rock.

34:28.171 --> 34:32.509
Some of us continued to search
for the meaning of those numbers

34:32.592 --> 34:35.011
while we waited for rescue.

34:35.637 --> 34:38.556
But then the sickness came.

34:38.640 --> 34:42.602
When my team was gone,

34:42.686 --> 34:46.106
I went back, up to the tower

34:46.189 --> 34:47.857
and changed the transmission.

34:49.025 --> 34:52.404
That distress signal we heard.
— yes.

34:52.487 --> 34:54.155
But the numbers...

34:57.200 --> 34:59.619
Did you ever find out
anything about them?

34:59.703 --> 35:02.122
Do you know where
they got their power?

35:02.205 --> 35:03.248
Power?

35:04.749 --> 35:08.878
They bring bad stuff
to everyone around you.

35:09.838 --> 35:12.674
They're cursed,
you know that, right?

35:13.633 --> 35:17.387
The numbers are cursed.

35:18.221 --> 35:20.724
The numbers are
what brought me here.

35:21.850 --> 35:26.104
As it appears, they've brought you.

35:28.064 --> 35:30.400
Since that time,

35:30.483 --> 35:33.778
I've lost everything,

35:33.862 --> 35:35.822
everyone I cared about.

35:37.365 --> 35:38.783
So, yes...

35:40.827 --> 35:43.163
I suppose you're right.

35:43.246 --> 35:45.373
They are cursed.

35:48.793 --> 35:50.920
Thank you.

35:54.716 --> 35:56.509
Thank you.

35:59.596 --> 36:02.307
You have no idea
how long I've been waiting

36:02.390 --> 36:04.434
for somebody to agree with me.

36:06.853 --> 36:09.230
Thank you! Oh, god, thank you.

36:17.280 --> 36:19.824
We need to find
Hurley and Charlie,

36:19.908 --> 36:21.534
get out of this jungle.

36:22.827 --> 36:25.121
I hate that we're
going home empty—handed.

36:32.462 --> 36:34.464
Someone shot at us!
Hurley and me.

36:34.547 --> 36:36.716
We were looking for you when...
— Rousseau.

36:36.800 --> 36:38.676
Where's Hurley? — I don't know.

36:38.760 --> 36:40.970
He was right behind me,
then he just...

36:41.054 --> 36:42.389
He just wasn't.

36:44.516 --> 36:46.810
I'll go and find him. — no.

36:46.893 --> 36:49.354
We'll all go. — go where?

36:51.648 --> 36:53.566
What the hell happened to you?

36:57.278 --> 36:58.405
Need a battery?

37:02.575 --> 37:04.577
She says "hey."

37:40.405 --> 37:42.198
You think of a name yet?

37:43.908 --> 37:45.702
For the baby.

37:46.703 --> 37:48.538
Haven't really thought about it.

37:52.792 --> 37:54.252
I was gonna give it away.

37:55.712 --> 37:57.922
You know, for adoption.

38:01.551 --> 38:04.554
Must've been a difficult decision.
— yeah.

38:06.931 --> 38:09.225
Well, doesn't matter now.

38:13.480 --> 38:14.939
It's my birthday today.

38:17.734 --> 38:19.611
Why haven't you told anyone?

38:19.694 --> 38:23.239
I'm pregnant, single

38:23.323 --> 38:25.867
and on an island
in the middle of nowhere.

38:26.493 --> 38:29.370
Doesn't really matter
that it's my birthday, does it?

38:31.122 --> 38:32.999
I guess not.

38:34.042 --> 38:36.669
Your birthdays will be close,
you and your baby.

38:36.753 --> 38:39.631
That's good luck.
— yeah? You think?

38:39.714 --> 38:41.174
Yeah, I do.

38:41.758 --> 38:45.678
You believe in that? Luck?

38:47.514 --> 38:49.390
I believe in a lot of things.

38:55.772 --> 38:58.149
Okay. I give up.

38:58.900 --> 39:00.693
What is it?

39:13.623 --> 39:15.208
It's a cradle.

39:16.751 --> 39:18.920
Happy birthday, Claire.

39:21.965 --> 39:23.174
Thank you.

39:34.185 --> 39:37.480
I know food's scarce,
but your shirt?

39:38.439 --> 39:40.817
When you find a laundromat,
let me know.

39:51.160 --> 39:53.830
Back in the jungle,

39:53.913 --> 39:57.250
before we became target practice,
you were gonna tell me

39:57.333 --> 40:00.670
what inspired this little quest.

40:15.018 --> 40:17.562
I think the plane crash
might have been my fault.

40:17.645 --> 40:20.857
Don't be daft. How could you...?
— before we came here,

40:20.940 --> 40:25.278
a lot of bad stuff used to happen
whenever I was around.

40:25.361 --> 40:28.406
What do you mean, like bad luck?
— yeah...

40:28.489 --> 40:32.452
That'd be kind of
a mellow way of describing it.

40:34.454 --> 40:36.789
Bad things happen.

40:36.873 --> 40:38.458
Planes crash. People die.

40:38.541 --> 40:40.209
You ought to let me finish.

40:40.293 --> 40:43.046
You think you're
the only person with baggage?

40:43.963 --> 40:46.591
You know what I was doing
when the plane went down?

40:48.217 --> 40:50.928
I was snorting heroin. In the toilet.

40:52.055 --> 40:54.724
I was such a junkie,

40:54.807 --> 40:57.727
I couldn't even take a plane ride
without having a fix.

40:57.810 --> 40:59.771
I suppose that was your fault as well?

41:08.613 --> 41:10.448
So how about it?

41:12.450 --> 41:13.785
What?

41:14.702 --> 41:17.080
I just told you
the biggest secret in my life.

41:17.163 --> 41:19.540
Thought you'd wanna reciprocate.

41:29.050 --> 41:30.218
Okay.

41:33.513 --> 41:35.181
Back home,

41:37.433 --> 41:41.187
I'm worth 156 million dollars.

41:51.239 --> 41:52.365
Fine. Don't tell me.

41:52.448 --> 41:55.118
Dude. — I bare my soul,

41:55.201 --> 41:57.787
and all I get is bloody jokes.
